      "protocol": {
        "compensations": [
          {
            "\"Different animals and datasets": "Liu et al. measured physiology in female flies and counted synapses in the female hemibrain v1.1; the counts here are from the male MaleCNS v1.0.\""
          },
          "The two rules rank pairs identically within one LHN type; they differ only across the six matched types, so the test has little power.",
          "Area is the whole neuron's mesh surface, one value per type; Liu et al. used a cylinder model of the whole neuron, about 8% smaller than meshes, and neither is dendrite-only.",
          "Holes in a published mesh are not closed.",
          {
            "\"Somatic uEPSPs of a cable neuron against a point model": "the axo-axonic VL2a -> local5 connection, smaller than its density predicts in Liu et al., stays in the primary set as in their main fit.\""
          },
          "Amplitudes below Liu et al.'s 0.2 mV detection floor are 0 mV."
        ],
        "content_sha256": "87a33e5fbc589f4445386618275c46bf88c18d7f97d46e1b02e82ff4535ef79d",
        "decides": {
          "not_testable": "fewer than 10 pairs with a MaleCNS count or fewer than 4 LHN types with an area, or any listed LHN type without a mesh",
          "primary": "the pairs listed under pairs: every pair of the six matched LHN types with a reliable estimate, zero amplitudes included, as in Liu et al.'s main fit",
          "verdict": "density if the interval lies above 0, count if below 0, undecided otherwise"
